{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Ten years ago on a cold dark night
[D7]Someone was killed beneath the [C]town hall [G]light
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
There were few at the scene but they all agreed
That the [D7]man who ran looked a lot [C]like me[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
She [C]walks these [G]hills In a [C]long black [G]veil
She [C]visits my [G]grave When the [C]night winds [G]wail
[G]Nobody knows [C]nobody [G]sees
[C]Nobody [D7]knows but [G]me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
The judge said son what is your alibi
If you were somewhere else then you won't have to die
I spoke not a word though it meant my life
For I had been in the arms of my best friend's wife
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
The scaffold's high and eternity near
She stood in the crowd and shed not a tear
But sometimes at night when the cold wind blows
In a long black veil she cries over my bones
{end_of_chorus}
